  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CRUDAN-Support to improving social cohen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will use localized and comprehensive integral approach such as community townhall meetings, community dialogue meetings, workshops, capacity building training and other relevant approaches. The approach  for engaging all members of the community will be represented in various categories (IDPs, Members of host communities, returnees, people with disabilities (PWDS), women, men, youths etc) on the path of sustainable development with the citizens being on the driver&#x2019;s seat leveraging relevant government and non-governmental structures in Borno and Adamawa State.  The project  will conduct and plan  activities as contained in the grant agreement including complementary activities approved. This includes project inception/technical kick-off workshop attended by all projectteam members; baseline assessment/wards analysis aimed at establishing the foundation for measuring progress throughout the project; comprehensive analysis of key sectors of focus. The proposed intervention will mainstream gender, social inclusion, and conflict sensitivity into the community plan to address both women&#x2019;s and men&#x2019;s needs and priorities, ensure full and meaningfulparticipation of women to achieve gender equitable outcomes.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="90">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Christian Rural and Urban Developme</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Christian Rural and Urban Development Association of Nigeria(CRUDAN) is a Christian inter-denominational, not-for-profit, Non-Governmental Organization. It is a membership organization that has as its members-Churches, Christian organizations and individuals that are engaged or interested in development work in Nigeria. It has the main goal of promoting the growth of the church in Nigeriaby assisting in rural/urban development work that is part of her witness. CRUDAN serves the church all over Nigeria in Wholistic development work. CRUDAN was formed in 1990, following the merger of two Christian organizations that operated independently in the country, namely Christian Rural Advisory Council(CRAC), Founded in 1965 in the Northern part of Nigeria, and Christian Rural Fellowship of Nigeria(CRFN), established in 1953, in the Southern part of Nigeria. Being a membership organization, the members from the general assembly that elects the board. CRUDAN has five(5) zones within the country namely, Central,Northeast, Northwest, Southeast and Southwest zones with a Zonal facilitator and Administrative Assistant for each zone. With this arrangement, CRUDAN is able to effectively cover the whole nation. CRUDAN began operation in 1991 and was officially registered by the Corporate Affairs Commission(CAC) of the Federal Government of Nigeria on 7th December 1992. Registration number 7111.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
